[Music]  since the beginning of breath of the  wild there have been glitches  most are pretty small simple ones that  people find as they uncover more of the  game but other times you watch as  someone does a multitude of random  things that doesn't make sense that does  something spectacular and you wonder how  did this guy figure this out well it's  almost always a group effort not just a  single person and even in cases where a  glitch was found by one or two people it  was often because of previous  discoveries that were found by even more  people these players share their fines  through discord youtube twitter and  reddit from all over the world in an  international effort one of the most  famous examples of this happening is the  difficult memory storage a complex game  breaking glitch starting a new file with  the all-powerful bow of light and all of  your equipment right off the bat in a  brand new game including the paraglider  which lets you skip the grey plateau  immediately so how did this come to be  how did this extremely complex sequence  get discovered let's break down the long  history of memory storage  let's first quickly explain what it  takes to let you walk around scot-free  with the bow of light to do this glitch  you need to have a cooking pot a travel  medallion a camera a compendium entry a  sheikah sensor plus a side quest and a  memory used together in a very specific  way then load a file and watch a memory  at the same time then die then start a  new game beat it without ever dying then  watch a memory again complete the game  continue an old file which starts a new  game instead then load another file  again  yeah it's a lot this in a very  simplified manner is what it takes to  perform this glitch the next question  would then be how did people figure this  out it absolutely makes no sense when  said in a list like this but there's a  method to the madness let's see how it  started  memory storage was found officially in  december of 2020 almost four years after  the initial release of breath of the  wild making waves throughout the  community but almost no one knows that  its origin was actually found three  months after breath of the wild released  back in june 24th of 2017 a speedrunner  named blue harvey found something  strange while casually playing he wanted  to continue his file in the cryoness  shrine and upon pressing continue  it works  it works the game instead started a  brand new file instead of loading the  previous save how does this work  how  what but not just any new file this file  carried over all this progress from the  previous file such as the doors of the  shriner resurrection already being  opened and this was the beginning of the  new concept of transfers this transfer  known today as flag transfer carries  over your game progress but not your  equipment while inventory transfer  carries over your equipment but not your  progress while this was only flag  transfer it was still a massive find  with huge potential that could lead to a  new game plus file and other glitches in  the future this was only possible  because the glitch blocked autosaves  from occurring but as fast as it came in  version 1.3  it was patched  six days later breath of the wild was in  its heyday with the release of the first  exciting dlc called the master trials  1.3 included the difficult trials for  the fully powered master sword and  various fixes to improve gameplay one of  these fixes was a new return to title  button and some fixes under the hood to  make sure the game would always  guarantee an auto save at the beginning  of the game while it's highly probable  that nintendo didn't even know about  this game-breaking glitch they had  inadvertently smothered this discovery  without ever knowing this glitch was  lost forever with no way to stop auto  saves from occurring right at the  beginning of the game and was slowly  forgotten in time  fast forward three years later on  december 10th 2020 whispers of a weird  glitch started to get uploaded to  twitter by a japanese user named shima  baka catching american player legend of  link's attention while to the average  player this looks like a bunch of menu  nonsense what's actually happening here  is the discovery of being able to hold  different prompts in different  situations outside of where they are  normally supposed to be such as with the  item menu or with champion abilities as  both of these players bounce around  ideas of new ways to hold menu prompts  the conversation moved to discord where  several people joined the discussion and  theory crafting including user kinok who  was experimenting with this as well  without getting too complicated using  things such as the shika sensor the  cooking pot the travel medallion and  pictures they could delay and manipulate  multiple menus at the same time  [Music]  the most interesting prompt though was  the memory prompt as it had more  promising outcomes than the other menus  so they pushed it more and more with the  dlc button with the options menu and  with loading files legend of link and  keynote continued to mess with file  loading but most fines ended with  nothing concrete only soft locks such as  being stuck on this black screen or  staring at a korok forever  but kinak finally noticed that in the  state of watching a memory then loading  a save anything after it will never  auto-save he wanted to take this  technique into the title screen and see  what he could do so he killed himself  then he went to the title screen and  started up a new game but something  strange occurred when he was able to  play again the game still never  auto-saved  this is when legend of link immediately  saw the potential of blue harvey's  legacy three years earlier so on  december 14th 2020 he connected a wii u  trainer to hack the wii u to do more  testing easily and went to work having  experience in this field messing with  file loading glitches before he knew  what he was doing and used hacks to  speed up the process of moving to each  place and only tried to replicate what  you could normally do on a regular  switch  [Music]  since he knew the game couldn't save as  you progressed the next logical thing to  do was to enable saving at the very last  possible time you could which was during  the dark beast ganon fight  after he did so he continued the game  and started up a fresh file but besides  the wall textures not loading nothing in  particular was abnormal until he saw a  curious game finish star on his file he  loaded up that save instead  [Music]  and successfully performed the first  inventory transfer using memory storage  in history transferring all of his items  from his previous file onto a brand new  game unfortunately this didn't have the  bow of light but theorized that having  it equipped in his hands as you beat the  game deletes it from your inventory so  he tried one more time with cheese to  speed up the process and  yes this was big  news spread of having the powerful bow  of light permanently and a new game plus  was discovered players flocked back to  the game spending countless hours  experimenting further and further  pushing the game more after this iconic  glitch only to find that this was just  the beginning of the craziness as this  led to things such as duplicating  colosseum lynels and spirit orbs  getting absolutely absurd amounts of  arrows  which could be chained multiple times to  get all of your arrows to ludicrous  amounts and even getting the ultimate  hylian shield with both max durability  and shield strength  every glitch in every game has its own  story and lineage some based on luck  some based on knowledge and skill but  one thing is for certain as long as  players are looking new and exciting  things will continue to be found if you  enjoyed this video let us know with a  like as we still cover the never ending  game of breath of the wild to this day  and for everything else gaming keep it  here on gamespot  [Music]  you

